<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Gorune - Tag - loommii</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/gorune/</link><description>我的个人技术博客</description><generator>Hugo 0.165.0 &amp; FixIt v0.4.5</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 16 Jan 2026 01:28:43 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/gorune/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Go Daily Question 216</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_216/</link><pubDate>Mon, 28 Apr 2025 00:31:44 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_216/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#10;&#10;import &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#10;&#10;func main() {&#10;&#9;i := 65&#10;&#9;fmt.Println(string(i))&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;A. A&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;B. 65&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;C. compilation error&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Reference Answer and Analysis: A.&#10;&lt;a href="https://go.dev/play/p/h8IE-NTMImR" target="_blank" rel="external nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;In UTF-8 encoding, the decimal number 65 corresponds to the symbol &amp;lsquo;A&amp;rsquo;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/details&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 160</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_160/</link><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jan 2025 12:22:18 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_160/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;Will they compile? Why?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;// 32-bit machine&#10;1）var x int32 = 32.&#10;2）var y int = x&#10;3）var z rune = x&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;1 &lt;a href="https://go.dev/play/p/9eGpGYkcqqp" target="_blank" rel="external nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;Can compile&lt;/a&gt;&#10;2 &lt;a href="https://go.dev/play/p/L5LsYs4NvDO" target="_blank" rel="external nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;Cannot compile&lt;/a&gt;&#10;3 &lt;a href="https://go.dev/play/p/xgIjiu6PQ1l" target="_blank" rel="external nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;Can compile&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 class="heading-element" id="analysis"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Analysis&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="#analysis" class="heading-mark"&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h1 class="heading-element" id="go-language-type-system-and-code-analysis"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Go Language Type System and Code Analysis&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="#go-language-type-system-and-code-analysis" class="heading-mark"&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h2 class="heading-element" id="1-untyped-literals"&gt;&lt;span&gt;1. Untyped Literals&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="#1-untyped-literals" class="heading-mark"&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;In Go, literals (such as &lt;code&gt;32.0&lt;/code&gt;) are untyped. Untyped literals can be implicitly inferred to the target type based on context.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 154</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_154/</link><pubDate>Tue, 07 Jan 2025 11:47:02 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_154/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() {&#10; i := 65&#10; fmt.Println(string(i))&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;A. A&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;B. 65&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;C. compilation error&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;A &lt;a href="https://go.dev/play/p/lYfJ6qOVMJV" target="_blank" rel="external nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;string(i)&lt;/code&gt;: In Go, &lt;code&gt;string(int)&lt;/code&gt; interprets the integer as a Unicode code point and returns the corresponding character.&#10;65 is the ASCII code (and Unicode code point) for the character &amp;lsquo;A&amp;rsquo;, so &lt;code&gt;string(65)&lt;/code&gt; results in the string &amp;ldquo;A&amp;rdquo;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/details&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>